  "text_md": ")\n\nTHE FACULTY OF SOCIAL SCIENCES of the University of the West Indies is pleased to be associated with the Institute of Caribbean  Studies at the UWI  Mona,  in  presenting  the Conference on Caribbean Culture, in honour of distinguished Caribbean Scholar, Professor Rex Nettleford.\n\nThe conference will be opened on Sunday, March 3, 1996 by the Rt.  Hon.  Michael Manley,  P.C.,  and closes with an address by the honoree on Wednesday,  March 6, at 8 pm.\n\n## PROG RAMMEcDRAFT)\n\n## SUnday, March 3,\n\nOfficial opening by Rt. Hon.  Michael Manley, P.C. 7 pm Venue: Phillip Sherlock Centre\n\n## Monday,  March  4th\n\n| 9am             | Plenary      | Social Science Lecture  Theatre (SSLT)    |\n|-----------------|--------------|-------------------------------------------|\n| 10:00  am       | Coffee Break |                                           |\n| 10:30. 12:30    | Panels'      |                                           |\n| 12:30  ·  2  pm | Lunch        |                                           |\n| 2  ·  3.30  pm  | Panels'      |                                           |\n| 4-6  pm         | Panels'      |                                           |\n\n## Tuesday March 5th.\n\n| 9am             | Plenary      | Social Science Lecture  Theatre (SSLT)    |\n|-----------------|--------------|-------------------------------------------|\n| 10:00  am       | Coffee Break |                                           |\n| 10:30 . 12:30   | Panels'      |                                           |\n| 12:30  ·  2  pm | Lunch        |                                           |\n| 2  ·  3.30  pm  | Panels'      |                                           |\n| 4-6  pm         | Panels'      |                                           |\n\n| Wednesday March 6th.    | Wednesday March 6th.    | Wednesday March 6th.                          |\n|-------------------------|-------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|\n| 9a